  "summary_en": "Brazilian bill PL 391/2026 regulates manufacture, sale, possession, use and software updating of humanoid robots. It mandates auditable programming, emergency shutdown, immutable logs and serial numbers, bans sales to minors and incapable persons, requires buyer training, imposes strict owner liability, and amends the Penal Code and Consumer Code.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Manufacturers must give government auditable access to functional programming; hidden or unsupervisable self-learning functions are prohibited.",
   "Mandatory emergency shutdown, redundant containment, immutable event logs and tamper-proof unique serial number.",
   "Sale or lending to minors, legally incapable and non-imputable persons is banned.",
   "Software updates require prior federal authorization; buyers must complete mandatory technical and ethical training.",
   "Owner strictly liable for damages; manufacturer liable for defects; new Penal Code art. 132-A with 4–12 years' imprisonment."
  ],
